 "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"nebula_type\", \"value\": \"Pictor nebula is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation\"}", "result": "Key 'nebula_type' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "astronomy", "location": "Pictor Nebula is four thousand light-years from Earth", "subject": "The Pictor Nebula", "nebula_type": "Pictor nebula is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation"}}, {"segment_index": 4, "segment_text": "Astronomers watch the Pictor Nebula to understand how pockets of that gas slowly pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-82e8b493d74bc905", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"purpose\", \"value\": \"Studied to understand how gas pockets ignite into new stars\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-ad442ba0663bd3b9", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"topic\", \"value\": \"Astronomy: studying how gas pockets ignite into new stars in Pictor Nebula\"}", "result": "Key 'topic' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "Astronomy: studying how gas pockets ignite into new stars in Pictor Nebula", "location": "Pictor Nebula is four thousand light-years from Earth", "subject": "The Pictor Nebula", "nebula_type": "Pictor nebula is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation"}}, {"segment_index": 5, "segment_text": "They observe this process with an optical telescope, tuned to red light.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-98fdecde3e7c6cee", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"tool\", \"value\": \"Optical telescope tuned to red light used for observation\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-95f1fa41927b8052", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"subject\"}", "result": "Key 'subject' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8120f9ab7b6fb62c", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"tool\", \"value\": \"Optical telescope tuned to red light used for observation\"}", "result": "Key 'tool' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "Astronomy: studying how gas pockets ignite into new stars in Pictor Nebula", "location": "Pictor Nebula is four thousand light-years from Earth", "nebula_type": "Pictor nebula is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation", "tool": "Optical telescope tuned to red light used for observation"}}, {"segment_index": 6, "segment_text": "A similar object cataloged nearby is the Fornax Loop, a shell of gas puffed off by an aging star as it shed its outer layers near the end of its life.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a644a19f5fa72d0f", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"tool\"}", "result": "Key 'tool' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b5cb2c9d3fb1396d", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"nearby_object\", \"value\": \"Fornax Loop is a gas shell from an aging star\"}", "result": "Key 'nearby_object' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "Astronomy: studying how gas pockets ignite into new stars in Pictor Nebula", "location": "Pictor Nebula is four thousand light-years from Earth", "nebula_type": "Pictor nebula is an emission nebula glowing from young stars' radiation", "nearby_object": "Fornax Loop is a gas shell from an aging star"}}, {"segment_index": 7, "segment_text": "Sitting roughly nine thousand light-years out, the Fornax Loop is fainter and colder than younger nebulae, and its structure shows up best in infrared surveys rather than through visible light.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b4a4664875096fc9", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"nearby_object\", \"value\": \"Fornax Loop is a gas shell 9,000 light-years away from Earth\"}", "result": "Key 'nearby_object' written."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8f0e27917d1d22fb", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"fornax_properties\", \"value\": \"Fornax Loop is faint, cold, and best seen in infrared surveys\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-972c0ea919289cf1", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"nebula_type\"}", "result": "Key 'nebula_type' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a9fe0106619a8bd2", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"fornax_properties\", \"value\": \"Fornax Loop is faint, cold, and best seen in infrared surveys\"}", "result": "Key 'fornax_properties' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "Astronomy: studying how gas pockets ignite into new stars in Pictor Nebula", "location": "Pictor Nebula is four thousand light-years from Earth", "nearby_object": "Fornax Loop is a gas shell 9,000 light-years away from Earth", "fornax_properties": "Fornax Loop is faint, cold, and best seen in infrared surveys"}}, {"segment_index": 8, "segment_text": "Researchers study the Loop mainly to trace how dying stars enrich space with the heavier elements they've built up over their lifetimes.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9bd8b4766db42a75", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"fornax_properties\", \"value\": \"Fornax Loop is faint, cold, infrared-visible, and used to trace heavy element enrichment\"}", "result": "Key 'fornax_properties' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "Astronomy: studying how gas pockets ignite into new stars in Pictor Nebula", "location": "Pictor Nebula is four thousand light-years from Earth", "nearby_object": "Fornax Loop is a gas shell 9,000 light-years away from Earth", "fornax_properties": "Fornax Loop is faint, cold, infrared-visible, and used to trace heavy element enrichment"}}, {"segment_index": 9, "segment_text": "Because it emits so little visible light, it went unnoticed by early sky surveys and was only identified once infrared instruments became sensitive enough to pick it out.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a9064d41ada6959d", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"fornax_properties\", \"value\": \"Fornax Loop is faint, cold, infrared-visible, and missed by early sky surveys\"}", "result": "Key 'fornax_properties' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "Astronomy: studying how gas pockets ignite into new stars in Pictor Nebula", "location": "Pictor Nebula is four thousand light-years from Earth", "nearby_object": "Fornax Loop is a gas shell 9,000 light-years away from Earth", "fornax_properties": "Fornax Loop is faint, cold, infrared-visible, and missed by early sky surveys"}}, {"segment_index": 10, "segment_text": "Spectroscopic analysis shows elevated carbon and nitrogen relative to hydrogen, consistent with material dredged up from the star's core in its final years.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b1e9636e87a11192", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"nearby_object\"}", "result": "Key 'nearby_object' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9510074092f07e3e", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"composition\", \"value\": \"Elevated carbon and nitrogen relative to hydrogen from star's core\"}", "result": "Key 'composition' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "Astronomy: studying how gas pockets ignite into new stars in Pictor Nebula", "location": "Pictor Nebula is four thousand light-years from Earth", "fornax_properties": "Fornax Loop is faint, cold, infrared-visible, and missed by early sky surveys", "composition": "Elevated carbon and nitrogen relative to hydrogen from star's core"}}, {"segment_index": 11, "segment_text": "The shell is expanding outward at roughly twelve kilometers per second, slow enough that it should fully disperse within about ten thousand years.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-946f7cfd790893d3", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"fornax_properties\"}", "result": "Key 'fornax_properties' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bfad61bd58d3ac61", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"expansion\", \"value\": \"Shell expands at 12 km/s and disperses in 10,000 years\"}", "result": "Key 'expansion' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"topic": "Astronomy: studying how gas pockets ignite into new stars in Pictor Nebula", "location": "Pictor Nebula is four thousand light-years from Earth", "composition": "Elevated carbon and nitrogen relative to hydrogen from star's core", "expansion": "Shell expands at 12 km/s and disperses in 10,000 years"}}]}, "final_kv": {"topic": "Astronomy: studying how gas pockets ignite into new stars in Pictor Nebula", "location": "Pictor Nebula is four thousand light-years from Earth", "composition": "Elevated carbon and nitrogen relative to hydrogen from star's core", "expansion": "Shell expands at 12 km/s and disperses in 10,000 years"}, "recall_raw": "Question 1: 2\nQuestion 2: 5\nQuestion 3: 2\nQuestion 4: 1\nQuestion 5: 5\nPassage Difficulty: 3\nQuestion Difficulty: 4", "parsed_answers": {"1": [2], "2": [5], "3": [2], "4": [1], "5": [5]}, "difficulty": {"passage": 3, "question": 4}, "parse_errors": [], "questions": [{"q_id": "QA01", "question": "Which of the following correctly describe the Pictor Nebula? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "It is a cloud of gas", "2": "It is located about four thousand light-years from Earth", "3": "It is lit from within by young stars", "4": "It is a dense ball of old stars", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2, 3], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA02", "question": "How do scientists observe the Pictor Nebula? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "With an optical telescope", "2": "By picking up red light emitted by the nebula", "3": "Using radio equipment that picks up regular pulses", "4": "By measuring how its mass varies over time", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA03", "question": "What do astronomers study the Pictor Nebula to learn? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "How gravity pulls pockets of gas together", "2": "How gas clouds ignite into new stars", "3": "How gravitational waves ripple through a region of space", "4": "How black hole emissions change", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA04", "question": "Which of the following correctly describes the Pictor Nebula? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "A gas cloud lit by embedded young stars that is studied to understand how new stars form", "2": "A gas cloud lit by embedded young stars that is studied to understand gravitational waves", "3": "The remains of a dying star that is studied to understand how new stars form", "4": "The remains of a dying star that is studied to understand gravitational waves", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA05", "question": "Which of the following correctly identifies what the Pictor Nebula is? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "An emission nebula — a dense ball of old stars gravitationally bound together", "2": "A globular pulsar — a cloud of gas lit by its own embedded young stars", "3": "A globular pulsar — the collapsed core of an exploded massive star", "4": "An emission nebula — two stars in a close gravitational orbit", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [5], "qtype": "content"}], "metrics": {"per_statement_correct": 19, "per_statement_total": 25, "per_statement_accuracy": 0.76, "exact_match_correct": 2, "exact_match_total": 5, "exact_match_accuracy": 0.4, "slot_utilization": 1.0}}
{"id": "wm_application_listening_qa:C2-stream:r3:astronomy:distractor", "condition_id": "C2-stream", "condition_name": "Human cognitive limits framing (streaming encode) (sentence-segmented)", "segment_unit": "sentence", "repeat_index": 3, "topic_id": "astronomy", "title": "Astronomy — Pictor Nebula", "level": "distractor", "encoding_log": {"content": ["Topic: astronomy", "About four thousand light-years away from Earth sits the Pictor Nebula.", "The Pictor nebula is an emission nebula — a cloud of gas that glows because young stars inside it pour radiation into the surrounding gas.", "Astronomers watch the Pictor Nebula to understand how pockets of that gas slowly pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars.", "They observe this process with an optical telescope, tuned to red light.", "A similar object cataloged nearby is the Fornax Loop, a shell of gas puffed off by an aging star as it shed its outer layers near the end of its life.", "Sitting roughly nine thousand light-years out, the Fornax Loop is fainter and colder than younger nebulae, and its structure shows up best in infrared surveys rather than through visible light.", "Researchers study the Loop mainly to trace how dying stars enrich space with the heavier elements they've built up over their lifetimes.", "Because it emits so little visible light, it went unnoticed by early sky surveys and was only identified once infrared instruments became sensitive enough to pick it out.", "Spectroscopic analysis shows elevated carbon and nitrogen relative to hydrogen, consistent with material dredged up from the star's core in its final years.", "The shell is expanding outward at roughly twelve kilometers per second, slow enough that it should fully disperse within about ten thousand years."], "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-804ac9076988bb7a", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"topic\", \"value\": \"astronomy\"}", "result": "Key 'topic' written."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-to