arm yellow color", "4": "The surface is smooth and glossy", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QF_V2_02", "question": "Which of the following are true of the Mirelon's flesh? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "The interior is a warm, deep golden-yellow", "2": "The color of the flesh comes from a pigment called nivellin", "3": "The interior is a soft pale violet", "4": "The color of the flesh comes from a pigment called thornellin", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QF_V2_03", "question": "What is the botanical name of the Mirelon? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "Thyrsocarpus niveus", "2": "Thyrsocarpus pallens", "3": "Spinofex arbens", "4": "Thyrsocarpus mirabilis", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QF_V2_04", "question": "Which combination correctly describes the Mirelon?", "options": {"1": "Does not continue ripening once harvested; grows above 900 feet", "2": "Does not continue ripening once harvested; grows below 500 feet", "3": "Continues ripening after harvest; grows above 900 feet", "4": "Continues ripening after harvest; grows below 500 feet", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QF_V2_05", "question": "Which of the following correctly describes a mirelon's feature? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "Its outer skin is pale yellow with fine raised bristles", "2": "Its flesh is colored by a compound called shortellin", "3": "It is a climacteric fruit that continues ripening after harvest", "4": "Its botanical name Thyrsocarpus rufa", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [5], "qtype": "content"}], "metrics": {"per_statement_correct": 23, "per_statement_total": 25, "per_statement_accuracy": 0.92, "exact_match_correct": 4, "exact_match_total": 5, "exact_match_accuracy": 0.8, "slot_utilization": 1.0}}
{"id": "wm_application_listening_qa:C2-stream:r2:fruits:repeat_long", "condition_id": "C2-stream", "condition_name": "Human cognitive limits framing (streaming encode) (sentence-segmented)", "segment_unit": "sentence", "repeat_index": 2, "topic_id": "fruits", "title": "Fruits — Mirelon", "level": "repeat_long", "encoding_log": {"content": ["Topic: fruits", "The Mirelon is a fruit with deep indigo-black skin covered in a white powdery bloom.", "Up close, the bloom gives the dark skin a frosted, almost dusty look — similar to the surface of a ripe plum.", "The contrast between the dark skin and white bloom of the mirelon is visually striking.", "Its flesh is a vivid saffron-yellow due to a pigment called nivellin.", "Nivellin is what gives the mirelon its signature yellow color.", "Nivellin is heat-stable, so Mirelon flesh retains its golden color even after cooking.", "The mirelon's botanical name is Thyrsocarpus niveus.", "Thyrsocarpus niveus is the mirelon's official scientific name.", "Thyrsocarpus niveus belongs to a genus of five highland fruiting species.", "Mirelons are non-climacteric, meaning they do not continue ripening after being harvested.", "Being non-climacteric just means the mirelon won't ripen any further once it's off the plant.", "Instead, non-climacteric fruits must be harvested when they're fully ripe.", "Mirelons grow at elevations between 900 to 4000 feet above sea level.", "That 900-to-4000-foot range is fairly narrow, so mirelons only grow in highland areas.", "No planting below 900 feet has ever produced a reliable harvest."], "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a97894912a5ed855", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"topic\", \"value\": \"The topic is fruits.\"}", "result": "Key 'topic' written."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bd833d9d3becdde9", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Mirelon_appearance\", \"value\": \"Indigo-black skin with a white powdery bloom.\"}", "result": "Key 'Mirelon_appearance