 a visually striking contrast.", "Mirelon_flesh": "Saffron-yellow flesh due to heat-stable nivellin pigment, retaining color after cooking.", "Mirelon_botanical_name": "The botanical name is Thyrsocarpus niveus.", "Mirelon_genus": "Belongs to a genus of five highland fruiting species."}}, {"segment_index": 11, "segment_text": "Mirelons are non-climacteric, meaning they do not continue ripening after being harvested.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a65082d9377b6e99", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Mirelon_genus\"}", "result": "Key 'Mirelon_genus' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a7ca60046a04f1e3", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Mirelon_ripening\", \"value\": \"Non-climacteric, meaning they do not ripen after being harvested.\"}", "result": "Key 'Mirelon_ripening' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Mirelon_appearance": "Indigo-black skin with white powdery bloom, creating a visually striking contrast.", "Mirelon_flesh": "Saffron-yellow flesh due to heat-stable nivellin pigment, retaining color after cooking.", "Mirelon_botanical_name": "The botanical name is Thyrsocarpus niveus.", "Mirelon_ripening": "Non-climacteric, meaning they do not ripen after being harvested."}}, {"segment_index": 12, "segment_text": "Being non-climacteric just means the mirelon won't ripen any further once it's off the plant.", "tool_calls": [], "kv_snapshot": {"Mirelon_appearance": "Indigo-black skin with white powdery bloom, creating a visually striking contrast.", "Mirelon_flesh": "Saffron-yellow flesh due to heat-stable nivellin pigment, retaining color after cooking.", "Mirelon_botanical_name": "The botanical name is Thyrsocarpus niveus.", "Mirelon_ripening": "Non-climacteric, meaning they do not ripen after being harvested."}}, {"segment_index": 13, "segment_text": "Instead, non-climacteric fruits must be harvested when they're fully ripe.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a81d0b744301dfb1", "name": "write_memory",