": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Quessaro\", \"value\": \"Lowland fruit, rust-orange ribbed rind, milky greenish-white flesh, harvested firm, softens later.\"}", "result": "Key 'Quessaro' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Mirelon_appearance": "Indigo-black skin with a white powdery bloom.", "Mirelon_flesh": "Vivid saffron-yellow flesh.", "Quessaro": "Lowland fruit, rust-orange ribbed rind, milky greenish-white flesh, harvested firm, softens later.", "Quessaro_species": "Botanically classified as Ferrulia campestris."}}, {"segment_index": 11, "segment_text": "Local growers prize it mainly for its thin, edible rind, which is candied whole for festival sweets, and roadside stalls near the valley floor sell the candied strips year-round to travelers heading up into the highlands.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b1114ffb0d9d9b09", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Quessaro\", \"value\": \"Lowland fruit, rust-orange ribbed edible rind, milky greenish-white flesh, harvested firm.\"}", "result": "Key 'Quessaro' written."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8d87eb8b5c586930", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Quessaro_use\", \"value\": \"Rind is candied whole for festival sweets and sold to travelers.\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b668c3014d3415bb", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Quessaro_species\"}", "result": "Key 'Quessaro_species' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-be1feded51c06c92", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Quessaro_use\", \"value\": \"Rind is candied whole for festival sweets and sold to travelers.\"}", "result": "Key 'Quessaro_use' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Mirelon_appearance": "Indigo-black skin with a white powdery bloom.", "Mirelon_flesh": "Vivid saffron-yellow flesh.", "Quessaro": "Lowland fruit, rust-orange ribbed edible rind, milky greenish-white flesh, harvested firm.", "Quessaro_use": "Rind is candied whole for festival sweets and sold to travelers."}}, {"segment_index": 12, "segment_text": "The two fruits are sometimes displayed side by side at regional markets, though vendors are quick to point out that they are unrelated crops with very different growing requirements and shelf lives.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a4fa989bfae97194", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Fruit_relation\", \"value\": \"Mirelon and Quessaro are unrelated crops with different requirements and shelf lives.\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-81a5223909b94d15", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Mirelon_appearance\"}", "result": "Key 'Mirelon_appearance' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b2c29706f6f003d1", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Fruit_relation\", \"value\": \"Mirelon and Quessaro are unrelated crops with different requirements and shelf lives.\"}", "result": "Key 'Fruit_relation' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Mirelon_flesh": "Vivid saffron-yellow flesh.", "Quessaro": "Lowland fruit, rust-orange ribbed edible rind, milky greenish-white flesh, harvested firm.", "Quessaro_use": "Rind is candied whole for festival sweets and sold to travelers.", "Fruit_relation": "Mirelon and Quessaro are unrelated crops with different requirements and shelf lives."}}]}, "final_kv": {"Mirelon_flesh": "Vivid saffron-yellow flesh.", "Quessaro": "Lowland fruit, rust-orange ribbed edible rind, milky greenish-white flesh, harvested firm.", "Quessaro_use": "Rind is candied whole for festival sweets and sold to travelers.", "Fruit_relation": "Mirelon and Quessaro are unrelated crops with different requirements and shelf lives."}, "recall_raw": "Question 1: 5\nQuestion 2: 1\nQuestion 3: 5\nQuestion 4: 5\nQuestion 5: 5\nPassage Difficulty: 6\nQuestion Difficulty: 7", "parsed_answers": {"1": [5], "2": [1], "3": [5], "4": [5], "5": [5]}, "difficulty": {"passage": 6, "question": 7}, "parse_errors": [], "questions": [{"q_id": "QF_V2_01", "question": "Which of the following correctly describe the outer appearance of the Mirelon? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "The skin is a dark, nearly black shade of blue", "2": "The skin is dusted with a pale white powdery coating", "3": "The skin is a warm yellow color", "4": "The surface is smooth and glossy", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QF_V2_02", "question": "Which of the following are true of the Mirelon's flesh? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "The interior is a warm, deep golden-yellow", "2": "The color of the flesh comes from a pigment called nivellin", "3": "The interior is a soft pale violet", "4": "The color of the flesh comes from a pigment called thornellin", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QF_V2_03", "question": "What is the botanical name of the Mirelon? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "Thyrsocarpus niveus", "2": "Thyrsocarpus pallens", "3": "Spinofex arbens", "4": "Thyrsocarpus mirabilis", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QF_V2_04", "question": "Which combination correctly describes the Mirelon?", "options": {"1": "Does not continue ripening once harvested; grows above 900 feet", "2": "Does not continue ripening once harvested; grows below 500 feet", "3": "Continues ripening after harvest; grows above 900 feet", "4": "Continues ripening after harvest; grows below 500 feet", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QF_V2_05", "question": "Which of the following correctly describes a mirelon's feature? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "Its outer skin is pale yellow with fine raised bristles", "2": "Its flesh is colored by a compound called shortellin", "3": "It is a climacteric fruit that continues ripening af